Let us conclude this section by pointing out that our implementation of~\A{} provides additional tools for \emph{analyzing polynomial evaluations} like
the proportion of leading monomials at a given evaluation point (see Figure~\ref{fig:decimationCircle1000Sph}).
Similarly, the localization of cancelations in the evaluation process can easily be deduced from the output files (see Figure~\ref{fig:estimPrecSphere}),
