  Given a memory $m : \mathcal{X} \to \mathbb{Z}$, we denote by $\llbracket e \rrbracket_m \in \mathbb{Z}$ (resp. $\llbracket c \rrbracket_m \in \{ \mathit{true}, \mathit{false} \}$) the value of arithmetic (resp. boolean) expressions.
  We interpret $\textsc{IMP}_\mathit{io}$ programs as labeled transition systems by giving a small-step operational semantics which, in turn, naturally induces a trace semantics.

