\section{Conclusion}
\label{sec:con}
We introduce a novel wavelet policy learning framework designed to enhance the precision and reliability of robotic tasks by utilizing multi-scale wavelet transformations. This method leverages lifting scheme to decompose complex, long-term sequences of actions and observations, allowing for a nuanced understanding of behaviors. 
% By applying a lifting scheme, our framework integrates smoothly with existing neural network architectures, ensuring that the wavelet policy is flexible and adaptable to tasks requiring high precision. 
% The detailed decomposition aids in maintaining consistency and accuracy over extended periods, making it especially suitable for complex environments.
% where traditional policy learning methods often fail. 
We evaluate method on five simulation environments across different tasks, and the experimental results are promising and demonstrate its potential
