\section{Ablation Study}

We conducted an ablation study on the her2st and STNet datasets to assess whether adding a third foundation model, UNI2, improves the performance on predicting cell-type proportions. UNI2 produces 1536-dimensional embeddings, equivalent in size to the concatenation of CONCH (512D) and UNI (1024D), and is trained on 200M pathology images using a ViT-h/14 architecture.

\cref{fig:albation_her2st,fig:albation_stnet} show CC and L1 scores across configurations: single-model (CONCH, UNI, UNI2), two-model (CONCH+UNI, CONCH+UNI2), and three-model (CONCH+UNI+UNI2). In many cases, UNI2 alone or the CONCH+UNI combination performs best, indicating that careful selection of embedding sources is more important than simply increasing dimensionality.

