\section{Conclusion}

We proposed a new pre-processing for the nonlinear detector structure, which demonstrates significant performance gain compared to the MMSE detector in scenarios with unknown interference. Moreover, the achieved detector is robust to channel estimation errors. Simulation results show that the proposed algorithm is quite stable with non-ideal channel estimation in both AWGN and interference channels, while the MMSE detector demonstrates BER saturation after the LDPC decoder. Traditionally, the linear detector is known to be the best solution for unknown interference scenarios or non-ideal channel estimation, but our results say that even in these cases performance can be enhanced due to nonlinear detector nature. Simulation results with modulation QAM16 and LDPC(144,288) decoder are provided for the co-located scenario with $64$ antennas of Massive MIMO: $16$ single antenna target users and $4$ interferers in the $3D$-UMa model of 5G QuaDRiGa 2.0 channel. 

