\section{Component Modules}
The quadcopter carries an on board computer running tightly-coupled modules: a YOLO-based vision stack that spots deer in real time, a coverage planner that issues energy-aware waypoints, an autonomous charging routine that handles return-to-dock and. Image frames flow from the camera to the vision module; detections and battery state are passed from the PX4 flight controller to the RL agent, which will decides whether to keep following the coverage route, initiate a deterrence manoeuvre, or head for the dock. 
