    Note that $\sim^{\alpha,f,g,\delta}$ is the information state \emph{after} the communication at time $\delta$, and that there is such a communication at every time $\delta < \alpha$. Hence $\sim^{\alpha,f,g,0}_a$ is generally not identical to $\sim_a$, since the latter represents the information state before any communication takes place.

    Furthermore, communication only happens at $\delta < \alpha$. Hence, in particular, if $\alpha = \omega$ then communication takes place at every finite time step, but there is no ``infinity-th'' communication at $\omega$.

