\subsection{LLM Agent and Knowledge Distillation}
\label{LLM_KD_section}
%  (Informed exploration) (Prompt design + CoT + bipartite matching)
% In the early stages of the RL training process, the random initialization of the model parameters results in poor initial decisions that do not align with common sense, and causes the agent to engage in a significant amount of meaningless exploration, which hinders the training process. The effectiveness of pre-trained LLMs as embodied agents in various decision-making tasks has been demonstrated \cite{Guiding,voyager}. Given that LLMs possess knowledge and capabilities that are aligned with human, they can be leveraged to guide and improve the early stages of RL training. 

