and some compressed sensing applications such as Single Pixel Camera \cite{spiv} and hyperspectral imaging \cite{ssec}.  
%It has been argued~\cite{cs} that certain images with $n$ pixels can be reconstructed with $O\left(\sqrt{n}\log^3 n\right)$ observations, i.e., $s = o(n)$.  
%
We also tried random inputs with $k = Cs\ln(n/s)$ for $C \in \{1.6,3,4\}$ and other values of $s$ in the range $[0.01n,0.08n]$.
