BenchOpt does not simply run a working set method $\mathcal{A}$ to completion.  It starts with a variable $i=1$, runs the first $i$ iterations of $\mathcal{A}$, produces a data point, increments $i$, and repeats the above on the same input. For example, %for the graph of working set size versus iteration, the data point produced is the tuple that consists of $i$ and the working set size for iteration $i$; 
a data point for the suboptimality curve is the tuple formed by the running time of the $i$ iterations and $F(\mat{x}_i) - F(\mat{x}_*)$.  
