%may suggest that the solvers are going back in time, but the reality is that the data points on a plot come from different runs.  
BenchOpt does not use the termination condition prescribed by $\mathcal{A}$; instead, it stops running $\mathcal{A}$ when the objective function value does not decrease for several consecutive iterations.  The final error is thus clear for comparison.  For clarity, we circle the data points in all graphs at which the corresponding methods should have terminated.   BenchOpt uses the smallest objective function value $V$ among all solvers tested and take $F(\mat{x}_*)$ to be $V - 10^{-10}$.

