\paragraph{Property 2: Injection.}
To prove that $\textsf{enc}$ (with respect to $\alpha \mapsto \beta$) is an injection, it is sufficient to show that the preimage $(x, y)$ can be uniquely recovered from the image $(\wh{x}, \wh{y})$ given $\alpha \mapsto \beta$.
