  To distinguish between these cases, let $h^\star = \{w_g,w_h\}$, where $w_g$ and $w_h$ are the vertices incident to edges $g$ and $h$, respectively. 
  The edge $h^\star$ divides $\wh{B}$ into two subpaths: $\wh{B}^g$, from $s$ to $w_g$ (with $w_g=s$ if $\wh{B}^g=\emptyset$) and $\wh{B}^h$, from $w_h$ to $t$ (with $w_h=t$ if $\wh{B}^h=\emptyset$).
