      \item If $s<t$, then $B$ forms a path, and thus $B=\wh{B}\cup \set{g,h}\setminus \set{h^\star}$ ;
      \item If $s>t$, then $B$  forms a cycle, and thus $=\wh{B}\cup\set{g,h,\set{s,t}}\setminus \set{h^\star}$. 
    \end{enumerate}
   To see this is correct, note that~\Cref{def:monomer-dimer-trans-path} specifies a ``flipping order'' for edges in $B= x \oplus y$. 
